# yfitops V2 — environment template.
# Copy to deploy/.env (gitignored) and fill in. Most vars map to a field read
# by server/internal/config/config.go; the VITE_* block is read by the dev
# launcher for the browser frontends. Defaults below are dev-safe; the server
# boots with all of them even if .env is absent.
#
#   cp deploy/.env.example deploy/.env
#
# Two consumers read deploy/.env:
#   - docker compose (deploy/docker-compose.yml) for production-ish runs
#   - scripts/dev-up.sh for the one-command local browser playtest
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DEPLOYMENT MODE — read this before a real event.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# YFI_ENV arms the default-secret boot guard in cmd/gameserver/main.go: the
# server REFUSES to start if ADMIN_SECRET, YFI_NONCE_SECRET, or YFI_JOIN_SECRET
# still hold the dev defaults below. (The guard lives in main.go rather than
# config.go because config.go is a locked contract file.)
#
# It fires whenever YFI_ENV is anything OTHER than dev — "prod", "production",
# "staging", a typo, whatever. Only an unset/empty value or exactly "dev"
# downgrades it to a boot WARNING. Casing and stray whitespace do not matter
# ("Prod", " PROD " all count as prod); an earlier version compared the raw
# string and failed OPEN on every one of those spellings.
#
# Leaving this at "dev" means the server will happily boot on `changeme-admin`
# with only a warning. Set it for anything attendees can reach.
YFI_ENV=dev

# Cleartext WebSocket fallback on /ws, for phones on a plain-HTTP LAN origin
# where WebTransport is unavailable (non-secure context).
#
# It takes BOTH vars below and is deliberately INDEPENDENT of YFI_ENV. Setting
# only YFI_DEV_WS=1 does nothing but log a NOTICE naming the missing
# acknowledgement — so if the LAN fallback "stopped working", this is why.
#
# Why not just key it off YFI_ENV: doing that made the gate mutually exclusive
# with its own use case. An operator who needed the LAN fallback had to stay out
# of prod, which ALSO disarmed the default-secret guard above — the flag meant to
# harden the deployment was pushing people into the weaker configuration. Now the
# two are separate decisions, and the risk is acknowledged explicitly instead of
# inferred from an unrelated var.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE SETTING IT: /ws has no encryption and no cert pinning. Anyone
# on the same network can read, forge and replay frames, INCLUDING the
# admin/stage secret in the hello. At a hacker conference, assume they will. Only
# on a network you trust; the real answer is TLS + WebTransport. Registering it
# with YFI_ENV=prod is allowed and logs a loud WARNING every boot.
#
# scripts/dev-up.sh and docker-compose.dev.yml already set both for you.
# YFI_DEV_WS=1
# YFI_INSECURE_TRANSPORT=1

# Path to the persisted Spotify refresh token. Defaults to a
# `spotify_refresh_token` file alongside YFI_CERT_FILE, which is what the dev
# server writes after the OAuth dance. Override only if the cert dir is
# read-only or the token lives elsewhere.
# YFI_SPOTIFY_TOKEN_FILE=/certs/spotify_refresh_token

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECURITY — change these before any non-local deployment.
# The three secrets below are what the YFI_ENV=prod boot guard checks.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Gates the admin / Control Room AND the trusted Stage screen (design_doc §9).
# Both clients must present this secret. CHANGE IT — default is a placeholder.
ADMIN_SECRET=changeme-admin

# HMAC key for the anti-cheat nonce gate (§4D). Any long random string.
YFI_NONCE_SECRET=dev-nonce-secret

# HMAC key signing the rotating QR join tokens (§3.1). Any long random string.
YFI_JOIN_SECRET=dev-join-secret

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SPOTIFY — REQUIRED for real audio playback.
# Setup (one-time, ~5 min):
#   1. https://developer.spotify.com/dashboard -> "Create app".
#   2. Add a Redirect URI EXACTLY equal to SPOTIFY_REDIRECT_URI below
#      (byte-for-byte: 127.0.0.1 not localhost, http not https, no trailing /).
#      A mismatch fails with "INVALID_CLIENT: Invalid redirect URI".
#   3. Enable both "Web API" and "Web Playback SDK".
#   4. Copy the Client ID + Client Secret into the two vars below.
#   5. The stage browser must be logged into a Spotify PREMIUM account —
#      the Web Playback SDK only emits audio for Premium.
# Without these the server still runs, but the stage uses a mock player
# (demo mode, no audio).
#
# Token lifecycle: access tokens expire ~1h after issue regardless of activity.
# The backend refreshes them via the stored refresh token and serves a live one
# from GET /api/spotify/token, so audio survives a multi-hour game — no action
# needed here beyond the credentials.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=
SPOTIFY_CLIENT_SECRET=
SPOTIFY_REDIRECT_URI=http://127.0.0.1:8777/auth/spotify/callback

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATA LAYER — defaults point at the compose service names. Override only if
# running the server outside compose. If unreachable at boot, the server falls
# back to in-memory store + a seeded sample board (see cmd/gameserver/main.go).
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
YFI_REDIS_ADDR=redis:6379
YFI_POSTGRES_DSN=postgres://yfitops:yfitops@postgres:5432/yfitops?sslmode=disable

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NETWORK / TLS — must match the published compose ports.
# 4433 is UDP (QUIC/HTTP3/WebTransport); 8777 is TCP (health/OAuth/cert-hash).
# Cert files default to /certs/*.pem inside the container; the server
# auto-generates a self-signed pair there on first boot if missing.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
YFI_LISTEN_ADDR=:4433
YFI_HTTP_ADDR=:8777
YFI_CERT_FILE=/certs/cert.pem
YFI_KEY_FILE=/certs/key.pem

# Concurrent WebTransport session caps (anti-flood; QA sweep 3). Defaults are
# generous so a NAT'd venue where many players share one public IP is never
# locked out — the per-IP cap targets a single abusive source, the global cap is
# the real resource ceiling. Set either to 0 to disable that dimension.
YFI_MAX_SESSIONS=2000
YFI_MAX_SESSIONS_PER_IP=128

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LYRICS / GAMEPLAY — optional tuning.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LRCLIB synced-lyrics source (§6). Public instance by default.
YFI_LRCLIB_URL=https://lrclib.net

# Skip-vote threshold percent of active users, 50-100 (§3.8).
YFI_SKIP_THRESHOLD=50

# Logical game session id used for persistence keys.
YFI_SESSION_ID=session

# Board dimensions. Loaded into Config.BoardRows/BoardCols by config.go, but
# CURRENTLY INERT — nothing in the server reads those fields (verified by
# grep; the only consumer of board width is admin.UpdateBoardCols, which is
# driven by the Board Builder UI, not this var). Setting these to anything
# other than the default does NOT change the board size. Left here
# documented-but-dead rather than removed, since config.go is a locked
# contract file.
YFI_BOARD_ROWS=5
YFI_BOARD_COLS=5

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI BOARD BUILDER (optional) — "Build with AI" in the board builder groups the
# track library into themed categories via Google Gemini. Without a key the
# feature is disabled (the endpoint 503s). Get a key at aistudio.google.com.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
GEMINI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.1-flash-lite

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FRONTEND (Vite) — read by scripts/dev-up.sh, NOT by the Go server. These are
# normally derived automatically by the launcher (host 127.0.0.1 + the ports
# below) and only need overriding for a LAN/remote setup. VITE_STAGE_SECRET
# MUST equal ADMIN_SECRET — the Stage authenticates with it (hello + the
# Spotify token endpoint).
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_WT_URL=https://127.0.0.1:4433/wt        # WebTransport endpoint
# VITE_HTTP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8777          # health / OAuth / cert-hash / token
# VITE_JOIN_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8780          # mobile buzzer URL encoded in the QR
# VITE_STAGE_SECRET=changeme-admin             # must match ADMIN_SECRET
